# Encoding and diff handling.
#
# Read this before adding a rule: the encodings here are mixed, and a wrong
# rule corrupts data rather than merely producing noise. Measured when this
# file was added:
#
#   Chummer/data/*.xml            UTF-8, no BOM
#   Chummer/lang/*.xml            UTF-8 with BOM
#   Chummer/settings/default.xml  UTF-16 LE with BOM
#   tests/fixtures/**/*.chum      UTF-16 LE with BOM
#   *.cs, *.resx, *.csproj, *.sln UTF-8 (180 and 78 files checked, no UTF-16)
#
# - the index stores LF, the working copy gets CRLF
# - an editor writing LF no longer turns into a whole-file diff
# - the one-off renormalize commit is listed in .git-blame-ignore-revs
* text=auto eol=crlf

# Later lines win, so the -text and binary rules below override text=auto.

# Saved characters are UTF-16 LE and are the regression corpus for the Phase 2
# golden master, where byte stability is the whole point. Marked binary so no
# future rule can capture them for normalisation - byte-level CRLF handling
# applied to UTF-16 code units would destroy them - and so git does not attempt
# a textual diff of UTF-16 that renders as mojibake.
*.chum binary

# Same encoding, same hazard, but small enough that a diff is still worth
# having, so normalisation is disabled without marking it binary.
Chummer/settings/default.xml -text

# - golden master baselines, compared byte for byte with the print
# - written with LF: a CRLF checkout would fail every comparison
tests/fixtures/prints/** -text

*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.pdb binary
*.suo binary

# Diff driver only. This does not imply the `text` attribute and changes
# nothing about how the files are stored.
*.cs diff=csharp
